"Kevin P. Neal" <kpneal@pobox.com> writes:

> Except isacfg doesn't seem to know about the wss0. I think I wiped
> the settings accidentally when trying to get booting from a CD-ROM
> working (long story, I'll post my defeat later). What are the
> magic settings for isacfg so it will recognize the card?

There is a script in the ROM called something like `add_sound' or
`add_audio' which recreates the isacfg entry.

In my machine, it's configured as:

wss0 at isa0 port 0x530-0x537 irq 9 drq 0: CS4231A
audio0 at wss0: half duplex

And it does work.

