On Sun, Nov 21, 1999 at 05:53:01PM +0100, Soren S. Jorvang wrote:

> some SRM revisions are known to have borked UDP checksum code.

Not the case, as I've said before -- you just need to use
"hn:vm=rfc1048" if you're using bootp, or "always-reply-rfc1048 on" and
"use-host-decl-names on" if you're using dhcpd.  My 3000/400 with SRM
7.0 boots just fine via dhcpd off my 5000/240.

